      "math_academy_id": "q-34634",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-5{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-3{b}_{2}+2{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-3{b}_{2}-2(-{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-3{b}_{2}-\\frac{2}{5}(-5{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-3{c}_{1}-\\frac{2}{5}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
